1
00:00:19,860 --> 00:00:24,260
Anyone without money, come to me!

2
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:29,000
I don't have any either, but don't worry.

3
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:36,040
Look at the blue sky, the white clouds!

4
00:00:36,040 --> 00:00:36,440
Me!

5
00:00:39,040 --> 00:00:42,960
Somehow, it'll all work out.

6
00:00:55,880 --> 00:00:59,920
Anyone without a job, come to me!

7
00:00:59,920 --> 00:01:04,500
I don't have one either, but don't worry.

8
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:18,260
Look, the burning sun...
Akanel too, it'll all work out eventually.

9
00:01:20,300 --> 00:01:27,460
You understand, right? Understood, understood.
Once you get it, shut up and follow me.

10
00:01:51,180 --> 00:01:54,900
Are the public bathhouses in Tokyo
really disappearing one after another?

11
00:01:55,360 --> 00:01:57,280
Now that you mention it, you're right.

12
00:01:59,080 --> 00:02:00,740
Somehow it feels a little lonely.

13
00:02:01,320 --> 00:02:03,780
Ryo-chan really loves the bathhouses,
doesn't he?

14
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:09,380
I love them too. That sense of openness,
so down-to-earth and approachable.

15
00:02:09,840 --> 00:02:12,300
Hearing it from Nakagawa, though,
somehow it sticks in my mind.

16
00:02:12,820 --> 00:02:17,700
Well, bathhouses were a social hub
for adults and a playground for kids.

17
00:02:18,560 --> 00:02:21,720
Back in the day, there were several
bathhouses in the same neighborhood.

18
00:02:25,700 --> 00:02:27,040
What's wrong, Ryo-chan?

19
00:02:27,900 --> 00:02:30,960
Yeah, I thought so.
This is the picture from that time.

20
00:02:30,960 --> 00:02:33,500
Senpai, you mean that time?

21
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:38,620
When we were kids,
there were bathhouses everywhere.

22
00:02:39,540 --> 00:02:42,140
Back when there weren't
many tall buildings yet.

23
00:02:42,560 --> 00:02:46,100
Bathhouse chimneys towered high into the sky,
one after another.

24
00:02:52,420 --> 00:02:55,260
Hurry, hurry!
Class One's guys will beat us to it!

25
00:02:55,260 --> 00:02:58,360
We won't let them get the Number
Three shoe locker at Nakajima's!

26
00:02:58,360 --> 00:03:00,260
The number one, the big one,
is hard to give up too.

27
00:03:01,600 --> 00:03:02,980
Yes! First in line!

28
00:03:11,820 --> 00:03:13,840
So the First-Bath Grandpa beat us to it.

29
00:03:14,580 --> 00:03:17,820
Well, it can't be helped.
They don't go to school or work either.

30
00:03:17,820 --> 00:03:19,580
Those are all retirees, after all.

31
00:03:20,760 --> 00:03:23,640
Still, Matsu-no-yu, Take-no-yu, Ume-no-yu,

32
00:03:23,640 --> 00:03:26,980
taking turns for first bath
at the Kotakeume like that.

33
00:03:26,980 --> 00:03:29,860
He really is a strange old man.

34
00:03:31,340 --> 00:03:34,720
The First-Bath Grandpa owns all the land around here,
you know.

35
00:03:34,720 --> 00:03:37,700
The bathhouse staff used to call him
"President,"

36
00:03:37,700 --> 00:03:39,760
but I wonder what company
he was president of.

37
00:03:45,920 --> 00:03:46,780
Well, that's about it.

38
00:03:46,780 --> 00:03:49,000
Put more soap on me, come on.

39
00:03:49,680 --> 00:03:51,000
Okay, ready to go.

40
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:53,360
Alright, then first up is

41
00:03:53,360 --> 00:03:54,700
Koichi, the great Chinkichi!

42
00:03:55,420 --> 00:03:56,640
Don't lose, Chinkichi!

43
00:03:57,260 --> 00:03:59,180
It's Furukawa's underwater tactic!

44
00:03:59,760 --> 00:04:00,780
Are you ready?

45
00:04:01,200 --> 00:04:02,100
Okay!

46
00:04:02,680 --> 00:04:03,740
Get set...

47
00:04:03,740 --> 00:04:04,540
Go!

48
00:04:05,720 --> 00:04:06,120
Now!

49
00:04:11,160 --> 00:04:12,460
Chinkichi, you cheapskate

50
00:04:13,980 --> 00:04:15,540
Teeeeee-!

51
00:04:15,540 --> 00:04:17,860
My junk got rubbed raw!

52
00:04:17,860 --> 00:04:18,940
Me too.

53
00:04:18,940 --> 00:04:21,680
The tiles are so bumpy, it really hurts.

54
00:04:23,480 --> 00:04:25,380
You guys are falling behind.

55
00:04:27,260 --> 00:04:27,800
Yoisho!

56
00:04:27,800 --> 00:04:33,000
If you slide with your junk up like this,
there's no problem.

57
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:34,840
I see, alright, me too!

58
00:04:34,840 --> 00:04:36,560
Okay, go whenever you're ready.

59
00:04:36,560 --> 00:04:38,840
Alright, I'm not losing!

60
00:04:39,820 --> 00:04:41,060
Round two.

61
00:04:41,060 --> 00:04:42,620
Masao versus Kankichi.

62
00:04:44,020 --> 00:04:45,900
We're going Mach 15!

63
00:04:47,240 --> 00:04:47,960
Launch!

64
00:04:49,860 --> 00:04:50,220
Amazing.

65
00:05:01,120 --> 00:05:06,700
The downside of sliding face-up was that
you couldn't see ahead and couldn't brake.

66
00:05:07,360 --> 00:05:09,640
You two should stop too, it's dangerous.

67
00:05:09,640 --> 00:05:11,440
Nobody's doing it.

68
00:05:11,440 --> 00:05:13,240
Ow ow

69
00:05:13,240 --> 00:05:15,860
Hey, you two again!

70
00:05:15,860 --> 00:05:18,780
If you pull this again,
I'll ban you from the bathhouse.

71
00:05:19,740 --> 00:05:22,760
Back then,
I went to the bathhouse every day.

72
00:05:24,720 --> 00:05:27,540
There was even a time I
stayed in for five hours a day.

73
00:05:27,540 --> 00:05:29,140
Five hours?

74
00:05:29,140 --> 00:05:32,780
The tiles were covered in grime,
and they just looked dirtier.

75
00:05:34,840 --> 00:05:36,980
That was right around that time.

76
00:05:37,543 --> 00:05:41,300
the whole school went out
to sketch at Shinobazu Pond.

77
00:05:51,560 --> 00:05:52,980
Ready, set!

78
00:05:54,420 --> 00:05:55,020
Nokotta!

79
00:05:55,140 --> 00:05:57,580
Go on,

80
00:05:57,630 --> 00:06:00,120
Tsuyoshi!

81
00:06:00,600 --> 00:06:01,580
Almost there!

82
00:06:01,980 --> 00:06:03,160
Kankichi, hang in there!

83
00:06:34,140 --> 00:06:36,160
Uh-oh.

84
00:06:36,160 --> 00:06:37,940
Uh-oh.

85
00:06:39,980 --> 00:06:40,260
Phew.

86
00:06:42,110 --> 00:06:42,980
Thank goodness.

87
00:06:42,980 --> 00:06:50,520
Eek! Sorry. It's fine.

88
00:06:51,880 --> 00:06:52,460
Mm.

89
00:06:56,800 --> 00:07:03,720
Wow, that's amazing and beautiful! Really,
I've never seen such a beautiful painting.

90
00:07:03,720 --> 00:07:06,020
The painting's beautiful,
but so is the lady.

91
00:07:06,020 --> 00:07:06,880
Idiot.

92
00:07:07,720 --> 00:07:09,360
It's called an impressionist painting.

93
00:07:09,860 --> 00:07:14,500
I love paintings like Monet,
Manet, Van Gogh, and Cézanne.

94
00:07:14,500 --> 00:07:17,220
Impressions? Gozanne?

95
00:07:17,340 --> 00:07:18,560
A comedian?

96
00:07:18,700 --> 00:07:21,800
Is he on Rock? I don't know him.

97
00:07:22,280 --> 00:07:23,720
I know Cézanne, though.

98
00:07:25,240 --> 00:07:26,900
That lady.

99
00:07:26,900 --> 00:07:29,920
Her name's Miki. Miki Orihara.

100
00:07:29,920 --> 00:07:31,460
I'm Kankichi.

101
00:07:34,660 --> 00:07:35,680
I'm Chinkichi.

102
00:07:36,080 --> 00:07:36,940
I'm Tonpe.

103
00:07:37,660 --> 00:07:38,380
Nice to meet you.

104
00:07:38,740 --> 00:07:39,100
Yes.

105
00:07:39,900 --> 00:07:42,800
Can we sketch next to you too?

106
00:07:43,220 --> 00:07:44,440
Teach us about painting.

107
00:07:45,100 --> 00:07:47,960
Sure, though I don't know
how much I can teach you.

108
00:07:48,520 --> 00:07:49,600
Let's draw together.

109
00:07:50,040 --> 00:07:50,400
Mm-hm.

110
00:07:57,780 --> 00:07:59,780
It's no good, I can't draw well.

111
00:07:59,780 --> 00:08:03,820
How do you get to draw as well as you, miss?

112
00:08:03,820 --> 00:08:06,540
That's because you're trying to draw well.

113
00:08:06,540 --> 00:08:07,740
Draw well?

114
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:09,420
Mm-hmm.

115
00:08:09,470 --> 00:08:14,180
For example, don't try to copy that
tree over there exactly as it looks.

116
00:08:14,660 --> 00:08:18,940
Just draw what you thought and
felt when you looked at that tree.

117
00:08:19,420 --> 00:08:21,960
What I thought and felt
when I looked at that tree

118
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:31,020
It's Kankichi's drawing!

119
00:08:31,680 --> 00:08:33,360
Wow! What should we do!

120
00:08:33,680 --> 00:08:34,640
Yay!

121
00:08:34,780 --> 00:08:36,280
There's mine too!

122
00:08:36,500 --> 00:08:37,520
Yay! That's my one!

123
00:08:37,760 --> 00:08:38,680
Yay!

124
00:08:38,760 --> 00:08:39,520
Yay!

125
00:08:40,100 --> 00:08:40,520
Chu!

126
00:08:41,120 --> 00:08:43,708
You kids, don't draw just what you see,

127
00:08:43,758 --> 00:08:45,980
draw what you actually feel.

128
00:08:46,360 --> 00:08:49,320
From now on,
call me Master Painter Kankichi.

129
00:08:49,360 --> 00:08:50,320
Ahahaha!

130
00:08:50,820 --> 00:08:51,280
Kyu!

131
00:08:51,280 --> 00:08:56,680
Good thing we did what the lady said

132
00:08:57,400 --> 00:09:00,180
But we haven't seen him around lately,
I wonder what happened.

133
00:09:03,460 --> 00:09:05,060
Today I'm definitely going to be first!

134
00:09:09,060 --> 00:09:10,540
It starts at five today.

135
00:09:10,540 --> 00:09:12,100
Why at five?

136
00:09:12,100 --> 00:09:14,800
They're repainting the bathhouse mural.

137
00:09:15,540 --> 00:09:16,880
That Mount Fuji painting.

138
00:09:17,380 --> 00:09:19,460
The paint fades from the steam.

139
00:09:19,460 --> 00:09:21,720
So they repaint it once a year.

140
00:09:22,560 --> 00:09:23,280
I see.

141
00:09:23,280 --> 00:09:26,780
Let us see it. Master Painter
Kankichi will give you some advice.

142
00:09:26,780 --> 00:09:28,520
Master Painter Kankichi?

143
00:09:28,640 --> 00:09:29,860
Just come on, come on.

144
00:09:36,600 --> 00:09:38,340
You're too slow. Bring it here quickly!

145
00:09:39,980 --> 00:09:42,640
Don't dawdle! The weather's going to change.

146
00:09:43,820 --> 00:09:44,840
Who the hell are you?

147
00:09:44,840 --> 00:09:46,280
Well, that's...

148
00:09:46,280 --> 00:09:48,980
It's not a fake, you know.
Get out of the way and go home!

149
00:09:49,500 --> 00:09:51,960
Tch, what's the harm in just a little?

150
00:09:54,360 --> 00:09:59,060
Hey, Kankichi, why is the lady...

151
00:09:59,060 --> 00:10:00,760
Run over here, come on!

152
00:10:01,600 --> 00:10:10,680
Mikki, Dad came up and said it wasn't good enough.
We couldn't find it anywhere, so I bought the same kind.

153
00:10:11,200 --> 00:10:14,100
We need that brush.
Could you look for it one more time?

154
00:10:16,740 --> 00:10:20,820
For a craftsman, tools are like hands and feet.
Hurry up and go find it.

155
00:10:24,920 --> 00:10:27,080
Miss, I'll help you look for it too!

156
00:10:27,080 --> 00:10:27,520
Thank you.

157
00:10:28,740 --> 00:10:30,080
That stubborn old man...

158
00:10:30,480 --> 00:10:31,600
He's my father.

159
00:10:32,320 --> 00:10:34,300
He's a total stubborn craftsman, you know.

160
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:45,720
Found it!

161
00:10:47,360 --> 00:10:48,260
This is it, right?

162
00:10:49,120 --> 00:10:51,060
Yes, that's the one.
I'm so glad you found it.

163
00:10:51,880 --> 00:10:56,060
But it's strange that he can only
paint with such a worn-out one.

164
00:10:57,400 --> 00:10:58,120
Yeah.

165
00:10:58,120 --> 00:11:01,220
Miss, don't you paint bathhouse pictures?

166
00:11:02,820 --> 00:11:06,060
My father thinks my
paintings are just a hobby.

167
00:11:09,120 --> 00:11:11,840
Rather than oil paintings
that please the rich,

168
00:11:12,900 --> 00:11:19,420
he says a craftsman's job is to paint pictures that delight
the customers who come to the bathhouse and the cinema.

169
00:11:20,940 --> 00:11:23,000
He takes pride in his work.

170
00:11:23,880 --> 00:11:25,300
So my paintings are...

171
00:11:26,740 --> 00:11:27,980
That's not true.

172
00:11:27,980 --> 00:11:30,480
Anyone who sees your paintings, miss,

173
00:11:31,500 --> 00:11:32,460
they're still not good enough.

174
00:11:33,220 --> 00:11:36,160
That's exactly why I want to
study oil painting seriously,

175
00:11:36,880 --> 00:11:39,040
and I'm thinking of
studying abroad in France.

176
00:11:39,440 --> 00:11:40,600
France?

177
00:11:41,840 --> 00:11:43,360
I'm absolutely against it, though.

178
00:11:43,920 --> 00:11:46,880
You can't make a living from oil painting,
you know.

179
00:11:47,460 --> 00:11:50,320
You don't need to listen
to that stubborn old man.

180
00:11:50,780 --> 00:11:54,420
You're such a good painter,
miss, so you should go to France!

181
00:11:55,340 --> 00:11:55,620
Thank you.

182
00:11:56,220 --> 00:11:59,180
Hearing that from you,
Kankichi, gives me courage.

183
00:12:16,520 --> 00:12:17,780
So what happened then?

184
00:12:17,780 --> 00:12:20,380
Yeah, do tell us the rest.

185
00:12:20,380 --> 00:12:24,000
It was the winter of that year.

186
00:12:24,800 --> 00:12:27,660
In the end,
she made up her mind to go to France,

187
00:12:28,260 --> 00:12:30,300
and confided it to her father.

188
00:12:31,380 --> 00:12:33,700
I'm leaving on the evening
flight the day after tomorrow.

189
00:12:34,540 --> 00:12:35,920
Thank you for all your help.

190
00:12:38,260 --> 00:12:42,320
Like Dad says, I may not be able to make
a living from oil painting my whole life.

191
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:44,740
But I want to give it my all.

192
00:12:46,140 --> 00:12:47,360
Have a trade in your hands.

193
00:12:47,920 --> 00:12:50,360
That's what my father always told me,
and that's how I've lived.

194
00:12:51,560 --> 00:12:53,100
I thought he was right.

195
00:12:53,640 --> 00:12:56,500
What's the point of painting
pictures that don't earn money?

196
00:12:58,820 --> 00:13:00,660
Don't you dare think you can
make a living from oil painting.

197
00:13:01,660 --> 00:13:03,540
I'm prepared for it.

198
00:13:06,300 --> 00:13:07,280
Do as you please.

199
00:13:12,780 --> 00:13:13,620
What?

200
00:13:14,860 --> 00:13:18,340
Big sis is flying to
France tomorrow evening,

201
00:13:18,780 --> 00:13:19,420
Really?

202
00:13:19,420 --> 00:13:20,060
Chi-Chinkichi!

203
00:13:21,620 --> 00:13:22,760
So, big sis is -

204
00:13:23,620 --> 00:13:27,460
apparently she's helping that stubborn old man at the Umenoyu first,
then leaving.

205
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:28,720
The Umenoyu

206
00:13:36,820 --> 00:13:37,640
Big sis...

207
00:13:38,900 --> 00:13:40,120
Kankichi-kun,

208
00:13:40,120 --> 00:13:42,340
Chinkichi-kun and Tonpe-kun too,

209
00:13:42,800 --> 00:13:43,940
It's you again.

210
00:13:44,360 --> 00:13:45,780
You're in the way. Go home.

211
00:13:49,180 --> 00:13:52,300
We want to properly
say goodbye to big sis -

212
00:13:55,200 --> 00:13:56,440
Kankichi!

213
00:14:08,580 --> 00:14:17,140
It hurts

214
00:14:17,140 --> 00:14:19,920
Dad

215
00:14:19,920 --> 00:14:22,360
It hurts

216
00:14:24,780 --> 00:14:26,020
I'm fine

217
00:14:26,440 --> 00:14:27,960
If it falls, stand the stepladder back up

218
00:14:27,960 --> 00:14:29,060
Keep going

219
00:14:29,440 --> 00:14:31,380
Damn it

220
00:14:37,280 --> 00:14:40,420
Dad

221
00:14:40,420 --> 00:14:41,620
Damn it

222
00:14:42,200 --> 00:14:44,720
We only have today off, you know

223
00:14:45,240 --> 00:14:46,720
We have to finish today

224
00:14:46,720 --> 00:14:48,700
We can't run a business like this

225
00:14:53,080 --> 00:14:54,260
I'll do it.

226
00:14:54,260 --> 00:14:55,000
What?

227
00:14:56,440 --> 00:15:06,480
Leave it to me, I can do it. Big sis is super good at painting,
and she's been helping the whole time, so she can definitely do it.

228
00:15:06,480 --> 00:15:08,660
Yeah, we helped too.

229
00:15:09,940 --> 00:15:11,100
Eeeeeh?

230
00:15:12,960 --> 00:15:13,320
Me?

231
00:15:17,020 --> 00:15:18,960
Let me do it, Dad.

232
00:15:21,140 --> 00:15:22,260
Eeeeeh?

233
00:15:25,400 --> 00:15:26,620
Dad.

234
00:15:27,980 --> 00:15:29,640
Do whatever you want.

235
00:15:33,520 --> 00:15:35,260
You stubborn old man.

236
00:15:35,260 --> 00:15:37,000
Thanks, Dad.

237
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:37,260
Okay.

238
00:15:50,620 --> 00:15:52,860
Up close, it's so huge.

239
00:15:53,460 --> 00:15:54,340
It's overwhelming.

240
00:15:55,020 --> 00:15:56,940
How many times bigger
than a 100-gō canvas is it?

241
00:15:59,700 --> 00:16:00,900
There's no time to hesitate.

242
00:16:01,800 --> 00:16:03,360
I just need to paint my own picture.

243
00:16:03,920 --> 00:16:04,240
Right.

244
00:16:04,980 --> 00:16:06,980
Mix the blue and green
paint more thoroughly, okay?

245
00:16:11,300 --> 00:16:12,900
No matter how much I paint, it won't spread.

246
00:16:13,600 --> 00:16:15,240
It's totally different from canvas.

247
00:16:16,260 --> 00:16:18,080
And the brush dries too fast.

248
00:16:18,700 --> 00:16:20,300
It's nothing like oil painting.

249
00:16:38,640 --> 00:16:40,980
I completely forgot about these kids.

250
00:16:43,280 --> 00:16:44,720
Wake up, Kankichi.

251
00:16:45,780 --> 00:16:48,180
Tonpe, Chinkichi, you too.

252
00:16:49,200 --> 00:16:52,640
It's already late.
Your parents will worry, so go home.

253
00:16:53,060 --> 00:16:55,240
Thank you so much for helping.

254
00:16:56,460 --> 00:16:57,960
Come on, we'll help until the end.

255
00:16:57,960 --> 00:16:58,340
But...

256
00:16:58,340 --> 00:17:00,860
Let us help. We want to help.

257
00:17:02,280 --> 00:17:07,800
Fine. But get permission
from your family first.

258
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:08,300
Okay.

259
00:17:09,220 --> 00:17:11,560
While we're at it,
we'll bring something to eat.

260
00:17:11,560 --> 00:17:12,300
And something to drink too.

261
00:17:26,040 --> 00:17:26,680
Okay, it's done!

262
00:17:27,860 --> 00:17:28,860
Yay, we did it!

263
00:17:29,580 --> 00:17:31,660
The women's side is done,
so next is the men's side.

264
00:17:31,660 --> 00:17:34,640
Right, there's still the men's side left.

265
00:17:35,660 --> 00:17:37,640
What should we paint for the men's side?

266
00:17:38,160 --> 00:17:40,320
Kankichi, what would you all paint?

267
00:17:40,840 --> 00:17:41,500
Mount Fuji.

268
00:17:41,900 --> 00:17:42,420
Me too.

269
00:17:42,420 --> 00:17:43,800
I'd go with Mount Fuji too.

270
00:17:44,340 --> 00:17:45,480
Mount Fuji

271
00:17:46,300 --> 00:17:46,620
Good.

272
00:18:01,280 --> 00:18:01,600
Good.

273
00:18:01,600 --> 00:18:02,220
Good.

274
00:18:18,080 --> 00:18:19,820
Two hours until the opening.

275
00:18:21,060 --> 00:18:22,540
We might just make it in time.

276
00:18:24,200 --> 00:18:26,440
Kankichi, get the red paint!

277
00:18:26,440 --> 00:18:28,800
We don't have any red left.

278
00:18:28,800 --> 00:18:32,260
Oh no, we need red!

279
00:18:33,700 --> 00:18:34,500
I'll go get some.

280
00:18:35,320 --> 00:18:36,740
Yeah, leave it to us!

281
00:18:38,300 --> 00:18:38,940
Thanks, please do.

282
00:18:47,400 --> 00:18:49,040
Mister, red paint!

283
00:18:49,960 --> 00:18:50,740
Red?

284
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:54,220
Miss is working hard,
but we've run out of red.

285
00:18:55,060 --> 00:18:56,180
Where's the red paint?

286
00:18:57,920 --> 00:19:00,360
Hey, mister, what about this red paint?

287
00:19:01,660 --> 00:19:05,160
Hey, kid! Bring me those two
reds from the shelf over there.

288
00:19:05,160 --> 00:19:07,000
And those empty cans too.

289
00:19:08,240 --> 00:19:10,380
I mixed that red myself.

290
00:19:10,380 --> 00:19:12,800
Nobody else can make the same one but me.

291
00:19:16,020 --> 00:19:16,620
Not yet, not yet.

292
00:19:17,600 --> 00:19:19,920
Okay, now! Mix it quickly!

293
00:19:20,380 --> 00:19:20,740
Good.

294
00:19:24,020 --> 00:19:24,500
The red...

295
00:19:25,320 --> 00:19:27,100
Kankichi, hurry!

296
00:19:30,660 --> 00:19:31,540
What time is it now?

297
00:19:31,840 --> 00:19:33,000
Around 2:30.

298
00:19:33,380 --> 00:19:34,280
We'll make it in time.

299
00:19:34,280 --> 00:19:36,880
Not like any customers will come
right at 3 o'clock anyway, right?

300
00:19:37,520 --> 00:19:39,060
The first-bath old man.

301
00:19:39,060 --> 00:19:40,940
Since he was at the Matsu-no-yu
the day before yesterday,

302
00:19:40,940 --> 00:19:43,180
to be honest,
today it's the Ume-no-yu's turn.

303
00:19:43,780 --> 00:19:44,560
That old man.

304
00:19:44,560 --> 00:19:46,460
If he can't get into the bath on schedule,

305
00:19:46,460 --> 00:19:48,100
he gets really angry, apparently.

306
00:19:48,100 --> 00:19:51,120
You two take this to the older sister.

307
00:19:51,120 --> 00:19:53,140
I'll deal with the first-bath old man.

308
00:19:58,640 --> 00:19:59,940
I'm not going to back down.

309
00:20:00,360 --> 00:20:03,840
Today's the Ume-no-yu, isn't it?

310
00:20:03,840 --> 00:20:06,980
Yeah, get it done so it's
ready at three o'clock sharp.

311
00:20:06,980 --> 00:20:08,100
Understood.

312
00:20:08,820 --> 00:20:09,700
There's no time.

313
00:20:11,980 --> 00:20:16,740
Alright, go for broke!

314
00:20:31,660 --> 00:20:33,100
I can't feel my arms.

315
00:20:33,600 --> 00:20:35,120
My legs feel like sticks.

316
00:20:35,680 --> 00:20:36,500
Hang in there.

317
00:20:36,500 --> 00:20:37,720
Miss.

318
00:20:37,720 --> 00:20:39,140
Just a little more.

319
00:20:41,280 --> 00:20:42,480
Just a little more.

320
00:20:58,460 --> 00:20:59,420
It's done!

321
00:21:02,300 --> 00:21:03,240
We did it!

322
00:21:04,580 --> 00:21:05,620
Three o'clock!

323
00:21:08,040 --> 00:21:09,360
Right on time.

324
00:21:10,680 --> 00:21:13,180
Alright, one last push, shall we?

325
00:21:17,640 --> 00:21:18,660
A red Mount Fuji

326
00:21:18,660 --> 00:21:21,060
Well, this is a magnificent sight.

327
00:21:30,360 --> 00:21:31,200
Dad.

328
00:21:33,620 --> 00:21:35,820
Look what you've done,
making it all bright red!

329
00:21:36,380 --> 00:21:38,620
Mister, go check the women's side too!

330
00:21:46,020 --> 00:21:48,360
From Japan, where Mount Fuji is, to France.

331
00:21:48,820 --> 00:21:50,440
This is how big sister feels.

332
00:21:50,440 --> 00:21:51,900
Both are wonderful.

333
00:21:51,900 --> 00:21:53,620
A fine feast for the eyes.

334
00:21:55,360 --> 00:21:56,400
Dad, I...

335
00:21:57,200 --> 00:21:58,500
The plane's time!

336
00:22:00,540 --> 00:22:02,560
I'll drive you in my car.

337
00:22:02,560 --> 00:22:03,920
Let go.

338
00:22:03,920 --> 00:22:05,020
Big sister, hurry!

339
00:22:06,140 --> 00:22:07,940
Take care of yourself.

340
00:22:09,180 --> 00:22:10,060
You'll be late.

341
00:22:10,060 --> 00:22:10,820
Go!

342
00:22:10,820 --> 00:22:11,680
Dad.

343
00:22:12,720 --> 00:22:14,200
Well then, I'm off.

344
00:22:20,240 --> 00:22:21,660
Big sister.

345
00:22:25,780 --> 00:22:26,960
Goodbye.

346
00:22:26,960 --> 00:22:28,640
Goodbye.

347
00:22:28,640 --> 00:22:30,060
Big sister.

348
00:22:31,620 --> 00:22:32,680
Farewell.

349
00:22:33,900 --> 00:22:35,180
Thank you, everyone.

350
00:22:48,660 --> 00:22:51,380
One day, a year later,

351
00:22:52,760 --> 00:22:54,180
Yes, first bath!

352
00:22:57,020 --> 00:22:59,240
Was the first-bath old man there?

353
00:23:00,360 --> 00:23:01,760
More than that,

354
00:23:01,760 --> 00:23:05,760
The painting's changed.

355
00:23:07,320 --> 00:23:14,140
It was a bit of a shock.
Only a little red paint remained beneath the painted-over picture.

356
00:23:16,040 --> 00:23:24,660
It felt like a precious memory had vanished.
I took it for granted, thinking it would always be there.
Only after it was gone did I realize how precious it was.

357
00:23:25,080 --> 00:23:27,960
Bathhouse painted murals
fade from the humidity,

358
00:23:27,960 --> 00:23:29,860
so they get repainted once a year.

359
00:23:29,860 --> 00:23:32,160
That's the fate of painted murals.

360
00:23:32,620 --> 00:23:34,900
So this photo is a valuable thing, isn't it?

361
00:23:34,900 --> 00:23:35,780
Yeah.

362
00:23:37,160 --> 00:23:43,120
Back then,
I regretted not keeping more memories of it.

363
00:24:18,300 --> 00:24:24,600
On a rainy afternoon, I walked looking back.

364
00:24:24,600 --> 00:24:33,980
Led by the hand of Gacha,
the strange feeling I had back then.

365
00:24:35,120 --> 00:24:45,320
So I tried walking on the arcade's tiles,
only on the black ones.

366
00:24:48,020 --> 00:24:53,580
Everyone was a child once,
but everyone has forgotten.

367
00:24:54,700 --> 00:25:01,020
Not the politicians with their self-important faces,
nor the blue-haired aunties.

368
00:25:01,520 --> 00:25:11,780
Turn that corner over there,
and you'll meet everyone.

369
00:25:11,780 --> 00:25:12,780
Don't go.

370
00:25:12,780 --> 00:25:16,460
There are turtles over there.

371
00:25:17,620 --> 00:25:19,800
Well, surely there are turtles.

372
00:25:21,200 --> 00:25:24,940
Everyone, come on over to our town.

373
00:25:26,080 --> 00:25:26,520
Thank you.

374
00:25:29,760 --> 00:25:32,680
I went down a road and found a gold coin.

375
00:25:32,680 --> 00:25:35,360
This must be a present from God.

376
00:25:35,360 --> 00:25:37,540
But then it turned out to be a prank camera.

377
00:25:37,540 --> 00:25:39,920
What's this, Chief, you're in on it too?

378
00:25:41,780 --> 00:25:42,920
You're not saying we're being fooled,
are you?

379
00:25:43,300 --> 00:25:46,160
Next time: Ryotsu Prank, Top-Secret Report.

380
00:25:46,670 --> 00:25:47,280
Nice to meet you!

